ULLIS(1)                         User Commands                        ULLIS(1)

NAME
       ullis - train compact ternary Hyena language models on Apple Silicon

SYNOPSIS
       ullis train --data DATASET --run DIRECTORY [OPTIONS]
       ullis tokenize --data INPUT --output OUTPUT
       ullis inspect --run DIRECTORY
       ullis generate --checkpoint CHECKPOINT --prompt TEXT [--max-tokens N]
       ullis chat --checkpoint CHECKPOINT [--session FILE] [--thinking LEVEL]

DESCRIPTION
       Metal is the default and intended Ullis training backend. It requires macOS on Apple Silicon. CPU is available only with --backend cpu and is for numerical checks.

       A training directory contains config.json (effective configuration), tokenizer.json (BPE trained from the input corpus), metrics.jsonl (append-only progress), and checkpoint.json (FP16-bit-exact model snapshot). Progress reports raw window loss and an EMA; use the EMA to judge a trend across different windows.

TRAIN
       ullis train --data dataset.jsonl --run runs/first --steps 1000

       --config FILE             Optional JSON TrainConfig.
       --resume CHECKPOINT       Restore checkpoint.json and matching tokenizer.
       --steps N                 New optimization steps. Default: 1.
       --learning-rate RATE      Positive stateless-SGD rate. Default: 1e-3.
       --checkpoint-every N      Save every N steps and at completion. Default: 100.
       --backend metal|cpu       Default: metal. CPU is a reference fallback.

TOKENIZE
       ullis tokenize --data raw.jsonl --output normalized.jsonl

       Validates and rewrites normalized JSONL before a long run.

INSPECT
       ullis inspect --run runs/first

GENERATE
       ullis generate --checkpoint runs/first/checkpoint.json --prompt 'Hello' --max-tokens 64

       Loads tokenizer.json next to the checkpoint and performs greedy t+1 decoding. It is a correctness-oriented decoder, not a sampling server.

CHAT
       ullis chat --checkpoint runs/first/checkpoint.json --session sessions/first.jsonl --thinking high

       Starts a line-oriented interactive loop. Commands: /think low|medium|high|xhigh|off, /save, /quit. User and assistant records are written as JSONL. Thinking level is prompt policy metadata; it does not yet impose a separate inference-time compute budget.

DATA FORMAT
       One JSON object per line:

       {"id":"demo-1","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"Be concise."},{"role":"user","content":"What is 2+2?"},{"role":"assistant","thinking":"Use arithmetic.","content":"4"}],"metadata":{"split":"train"}}

       Allowed roles: system, user, assistant, tool. Every assistant message requires a non-empty thinking field. Tool messages require tool_call_id. Optional assistant tool_calls have {id, name, arguments}; this reserves the future agent-trace schema but does not execute tools.

FILES
       examples/first-train.jsonl  Minimal wiring dataset, not a useful corpus.

EXIT STATUS
       0      Command completed successfully.
       non-0  Invalid dataset/configuration, unavailable Metal device, or I/O failure.
